From 6e5501a7e560fb6a2b406d9d83c19d6f8ad42d5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agents-factory-impl-l2xb <agents-factory-impl-l2xb@exe.xyz>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:45:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fleet-land-message): derive the branch author from the
 branch, and let the lander supply the authoring model (agents-2tov)

Rebased onto the APPLIED STATE (live + fleet-verdict-transcription-scanner + fleet-verdict-model-families-filter +
fleet-verdict-pool-sha-relevance), which is the order the hub applies these patches in and therefore the base this
patch must be cut against.

The independence check took the "branch author" from the ACTOR of the operative LAND-SUMMARY comment. A summary
appended by another lane - a coordinator replacing a block whose author's bd writes were timing out, a workflow
the helper explicitly supports - therefore made the APPENDER the author, and the comparison used the appender's
family: on agents-jb8m a deepseek reviewer was refused as same-family against coord's record while the branch's
own lane (impl-f6du) reads openai-codex/gpt-6-sol, i.e. genuinely cross-family. THE SAME WRONG OBJECT IS WORSE IN
THE OTHER DIRECTION: the author-lane verdict filter discounted the APPENDER's verdicts, so with an appender of a
different family the AUTHOR's own verdict counts as independent evidence - a false POSITIVE, which authorises a
landing, rather than a false negative, which merely blocks one.

The author is now derived from the BRANCH NAME (fleet/<lane>-<bead> -> the longest lane recorded in
~/.fleet/lanes/*.model that matches at a boundary), with the operative summary's actor kept only as a labelled
fallback, and the derivation's SOURCE is recorded (author_lane, author_source, author_model_source in
--print-json; named in the refusal text). When no object settles the authoring model, --author-model supplies the
OPERAND rather than overriding the rule: the comparison still runs, the value is recorded as supplied, and the
refusal names that flag as the remedy.

On this base the pre-rank filter block the patch carried against plain live is deliberately NOT reintroduced:
the rank-scoped pool patch supersedes it. The test case is 38 (the scanner owns 36 and the pool patch owns 37),
and 38j asserts the demotion by which verdict is SELECTED rather than by author_lane_verdicts_ignored, which is 0
in that fixture under the rank-scoped pool.

Verified on this base: tests/fleet-land-message.test.sh 341 passed / 0 failed. Against the base WITHOUT this
change the new case fails (the fixture produces no such JSON at all) while the other patches' 324 assertions pass.
